{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019DcvpuD9SdcKoSAghikLMX","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"ACL ARR 2026 reviewer guidelines scoring criteria\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"ARR Area Chair Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/acguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"CALL FOR PAPERS – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/cfp\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Reviewer Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"aclrollingreview/cfp.md at main · acl-org/aclrollingreview\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/acl-org/aclrollingreview/blob/main/cfp.md\"},{\"title\":\"aclrollingreview/reviewing.md at main · acl-org/aclrollingreview\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/acl-org/aclrollingreview/blob/main/reviewing.md\"},{\"title\":\"How ARR works – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewing\"},{\"title\":\"Authors Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/authors\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here are the key details about ACL ARR 2026 reviewer guidelines and scoring criteria:\n\n## Reviewer Scoring Criteria\n\nStarting with February 2025, ARR reviewers are asked to provide three scores: soundness, excitement, and overall recommendation.\n\n### Soundness Score\nIf you give a low Soundness score without finding any major faults, this means that your review is not a faithful explanation of your recommendation, and you need to revise it. All papers recommended for Findings or main conference are expected to be sound and reproducible.\n\n### Excitement Score\nSometimes you may find the work sound, but not something that is interesting for you personally. Such preferences are more subjective and should be reflected in a separate excitement score, which is orthogonal to the assessment of the soundness of the paper.\n\n### Overall Assessment Score\nThe Overall assessment score is an explicit recommendation for the outcome of this paper, if it were committed to an *ACL venue.\n\n## General Reviewing Principles\n\nARR reviewers are instructed to write a review as if the paper were being considered for the ACL conference. Thus low scores may indicate the submission is not a good fit for ACL, even if it may be a good fit for other/more specialized venues.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e2f100d3-931f-4e74-a45a-f78f1352b916","uuid":"9b9a13dd-e3d6-40de-bbaf-ae1ba7f70410","timestamp":"2026-05-21T05:49:49.569Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"ACL ARR 2026 reviewer guidelines scoring criteria","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01LvfCXj2ip3LSNvZKk8h5Nx","content":[{"title":"ARR Area Chair Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/acguidelines"},{"title":"CALL FOR PAPERS – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/cfp"},{"title":"ARR Reviewer Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines"},{"title":"aclrollingreview/cfp.md at main · acl-org/aclrollingreview","url":"https://github.com/acl-org/aclrollingreview/blob/main/cfp.md"},{"title":"aclrollingreview/reviewing.md at main · acl-org/aclrollingreview","url":"https://github.com/acl-org/aclrollingreview/blob/main/reviewing.md"},{"title":"How ARR works – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewing"},{"title":"Authors Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/authors"}]},"Based on the search results, here are the key details about ACL ARR 2026 reviewer guidelines and scoring criteria:\n\n## Reviewer Scoring Criteria\n\nStarting with February 2025, ARR reviewers are asked to provide three scores: soundness, excitement, and overall recommendation.\n\n### Soundness Score\nIf you give a low Soundness score without finding any major faults, this means that your review is not a faithful explanation of your recommendation, and you need to revise it. All papers recommended for Findings or main conference are expected to be sound and reproducible.\n\n### Excitement Score\nSometimes you may find the work sound, but not something that is interesting for you personally. Such preferences are more subjective and should be reflected in a separate excitement score, which is orthogonal to the assessment of the soundness of the paper.\n\n### Overall Assessment Score\nThe Overall assessment score is an explicit recommendation for the outcome of this paper, if it were committed to an *ACL venue.\n\n## General Reviewing Principles\n\nARR reviewers are instructed to write a review as if the paper were being considered for the ACL conference. Thus low scores may indicate the submission is not a good fit for ACL, even if it may be a good fit for other/more specialized venues."],"durationSeconds":7.975447190999999}}
