{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01S22iYyQGKZsQzj9Xzkw32Z","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"ACL Rolling Review reviewer scoring rubric soundness excitement overall assessment 1-5 scale 2025 2026\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"aclrollingreview/reviewerguidelines.md at main · acl-org/aclrollingreview\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/acl-org/aclrollingreview/blob/main/reviewerguidelines.md\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Reviewer Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Area Chair Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/acguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"ACL’23 Peer Review Form - ACL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://2023.aclweb.org/blog/review-form/\"},{\"title\":\"ACL 2023 Acceptance Recommendations - ACL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://2023.aclweb.org/blog/overall-recommendation/\"},{\"title\":\"Program Chairs’ Report on Peer Review at ACL 2023 Anna Rogers}\",\"url\":\"https://aclanthology.org/2023.acl-long.report.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"ACL’23 Peer Review Policies - ACL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://2023.aclweb.org/blog/review-acl23/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about the ACL Rolling Review (ARR) reviewer scoring rubric:\n\n## Scoring Components\n\nStarting with February 2025, ARR reviewers are asked to provide three scores: soundness, excitement, and overall recommendation.\n\n## Soundness Score\n\nThe soundness scores must be justified by the text of the review. Soundness goes to how well the paper clearly states its claims and backs up them with evidence and argumentation. If you give a low Soundness score without finding any major faults, this means that your review is not a faithful explanation of your recommendation, and you need to revise it.\n\n## Excitement Score\n\nSometimes you may find the work sound, but not something that is interesting for you personally. Such preferences are more subjective and should be reflected in a separate excitement score, which is orthogonal to the assessment of the soundness of the paper.\n\n## Overall Assessment Score\n\nThe Overall assessment score is an explicit recommendation for the outcome of this paper, if it were committed to an *ACL venue. This is a composite score reflecting your assessment of soundness, excitement, and also other factors like novelty and impact.\n\nThe search results confirm these three scoring categories for 2025 onwards, though the specific 1-5 scale definitions are not detailed in the current ARR guidelines provided.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e2f100d3-931f-4e74-a45a-f78f1352b916","uuid":"d1979364-2e7e-43f4-821a-d4a1cba0db43","timestamp":"2026-05-21T05:50:08.745Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"ACL Rolling Review reviewer scoring rubric soundness excitement overall assessment 1-5 scale 2025 2026","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01Tq4ZZKTaBDFATghxNr1keV","content":[{"title":"aclrollingreview/reviewerguidelines.md at main · acl-org/aclrollingreview","url":"https://github.com/acl-org/aclrollingreview/blob/main/reviewerguidelines.md"},{"title":"ARR Reviewer Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines"},{"title":"ARR Area Chair Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/acguidelines"},{"title":"ACL’23 Peer Review Form - ACL 2023","url":"https://2023.aclweb.org/blog/review-form/"},{"title":"ACL 2023 Acceptance Recommendations - ACL 2023","url":"https://2023.aclweb.org/blog/overall-recommendation/"},{"title":"Program Chairs’ Report on Peer Review at ACL 2023 Anna Rogers}","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2023.acl-long.report.pdf"},{"title":"ACL’23 Peer Review Policies - ACL 2023","url":"https://2023.aclweb.org/blog/review-acl23/"}]},"Based on the search results, here's what I found about the ACL Rolling Review (ARR) reviewer scoring rubric:\n\n## Scoring Components\n\nStarting with February 2025, ARR reviewers are asked to provide three scores: soundness, excitement, and overall recommendation.\n\n## Soundness Score\n\nThe soundness scores must be justified by the text of the review. Soundness goes to how well the paper clearly states its claims and backs up them with evidence and argumentation. If you give a low Soundness score without finding any major faults, this means that your review is not a faithful explanation of your recommendation, and you need to revise it.\n\n## Excitement Score\n\nSometimes you may find the work sound, but not something that is interesting for you personally. Such preferences are more subjective and should be reflected in a separate excitement score, which is orthogonal to the assessment of the soundness of the paper.\n\n## Overall Assessment Score\n\nThe Overall assessment score is an explicit recommendation for the outcome of this paper, if it were committed to an *ACL venue. This is a composite score reflecting your assessment of soundness, excitement, and also other factors like novelty and impact.\n\nThe search results confirm these three scoring categories for 2025 onwards, though the specific 1-5 scale definitions are not detailed in the current ARR guidelines provided."],"durationSeconds":6.637107006999999}}
